Abstract = {Road safety is a major problem nowadays due to its vast socioeconomic
   impacts. Enforcement and rehabilitation measures have been applied
   widely in many countries in order to achieve improved driver behaviour.
   Among the administrative support systems of the competent authorities as
   far as road safety is concerned, the penalty point system plays an
   important role in behavioural changes. Greece is among those countries
   facing severe road safety problems and for this reason a major effort
   has been made towards the improvement of safety levels in the country.
   Within the framework of this paper the Greek point system is presented
   and discussed in relation to the country's road accident data.},
