   \& TECHNOL; COMMISS EUROPEAN COMMUNITIES; EUROPEAN CONF MINISTERS
   TRANSPORT; FRENCH DEPT RES \& ENVIRONM},
Abstract = {This paper describes the prospects of improving the air pollution
   situation in urban areas by means of traffic control measures introduced
   under different emission control scenarios. A major feature of this work
   consists of test modelling studies applied in the region of Athens. The
   required reduction in traffic levels was found to vary according to the
   scenario and emission control alternatives. Evidence suggests that
   emission control systems may be less effective than anticipated due to
   prevailing traffic conditions and deterioration with use. These factors
   would lead to underestimation of emissions and the resultant
   concentration of pollutants. The advocated approach is based on
   source-receptor relationships and surveillance plans using information
   technologies.},
