Organization = {ICIB-CNR; IISF; Reg Campan; eBSA; AI{*}IA; GIRPR; SIBPA; SINS},
Abstract = {The paper addresses experimental results on peri-space geometry and
   topology perception with a touch sense. A dedicated
   ``perception-action{''} platform, involving artificial vision and a hand
   tactile stimulation device as well as convenient touch-space perception
   experiments have been designed. The proposed gravitation representation
   of the space is based upon nearest object edge displays on tactile
   device, which dynamically modifies with subject navigating in the plate
   form. This representation has been evaluated on voluntary blindfolded
   healthy male and female subjects. The collected data show that it is
   possible to navigate in space using the touch stimulating device.},
