   BIOSCIENCE (ICFEEB 2013)},
Year = {2013},
Pages = {577-583},
Note = {International Conference on Frontiers of Environment, Energy and
   Bioscience (ICFEEB), Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 24-25, 2013},
Abstract = {Municipal solid waste issue has significant impacts to human sustainable
   development. In China, many middle and small cities attempt to optimize
   their MSW systems through combination of the appropriate collecting,
   transporting and treatment models in order to meets their sustainable
   goals. This research, based on the case of Zhangqiu City, develops five
   realistic scenarios: the current (baseline) situation, mixed separation
   plus sanitary landfill with LFG and leathate collection; mixed
   collection plus waste to energy incineration; separated collection plus
   compost/biogasfication; separated collection plus compost/biogasfication
   and waste to energy incineration (Synthesized treatments); which
   represent the most prevailing municipal solid waste management
   approaches available in China cities. Then, evaluate and compare the
   environmental impacts of these scenarios through life cycle inventories
   (LCI) method.},
