Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper introduces a methodology based on the Geographical
   Information System to quantify reservoirs siting up using the Manso
   River Reservoir System as a case study. The Manso's System is one of the
   two most important water reservoirs serving the Belo Horizonte City
   urban area, in Minas Gerais State, Brazil. The 1991's city water demand
   was 8.24m(3)/s and its 2005's water demand is expected to be of 15,66
   m(3)/s. The Manso System was first operational in 1991, displaying the
   following characteristics: reservoir volume of 120 x 10(6) m(3), basin
   area of 670 km(2), cost of US\$550,000,000 and expected silting up
   annual rate of 3.25 x 10(6) m(3). The resulting data support that the
   reservoir silting up annual rate was underestimated by a factor of
   almost nine, anticipating that the reservoir capacity could be exhausted
   by 2005.},
