   Hong Kong Inst Util Specialists},
Abstract = {Construction waste has wide-ranging impacts on the environment,
   community and economy. Excessive generation of construction waste
   without proper control and management could cause pollution to the
   environment. Barriers to good waste management practices add weakness to
   the construction waste control system. This paper presents the current
   status of construction waste control system in Ipoh, Malaysia. Through a
   series of site audit, this study has identified several barriers to good
   waste management practices faced at construction sites including level
   of knowledge, waste operational costs and lack of guidelines by the
   local authority. Recommendations are made in order to improve
   construction waste management in Ipoh based on the strengths, weakness,
   opportunities and threats of the current waste control system.},
