   Hospitality Management and Education Session, Berlin, GERMANY, JUN
   15-18, 2012},
Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {At present, education for children from immigrant workers is a
   significant social problem along with urban development in China, which
   may affect social harmony, stability and social economic development. In
   this paper, the author analyzes the macro background of problems
   associated with immigrant workers' children education from the
   perspective of new public management, and points out that public primary
   and secondary schools cannot meet the education needs of migrant
   workers' children. This may result from failures from the government and
   market. In order to solve such problems, the author proposes a school
   running mode which takes the NPO as the main body with government
   supports, community involvement, corporate contributions, and media
   attention. At the end of the paper, external risk was also displayed
   associated with the public welfare running mode.},
