   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {This article describes the features of the ``social and professional
   security{''} young professionals in enterprises and institutions in the
   course of their professional adaptation.
   For a more comprehensive discussion of this topic is given by the
   definition of ``young professional{''}. ``Social -professional
   ``security in relation to the young specialist is a series of measures
   aimed at the protection and realization of their professional
   activities, guarantees and rights. Adaptation problem of young people
   who begin their career is activated in the modern era of innovation.
   Professional adaptation - is a process of adaptation to the activities
   directly dependent on the professional identification - career
   development. For the formation and implementation of this type of
   identification are required technological and psychological conditions
   of the special knowledge of, and compliance with the abilities of the
   young specialist nature of professional activity. Professional
   identification is associated with the implementation of a young
   specialist functional responsibilities, as well as his participation in
   the activities of scientific and technical societies, scientific and
   technical conferences.
   To expedite the process of adaptation to the young specialist is used
   sonic measures, which include: the appointment of a mentor to the young
   person who tells a new employee that he will do as it will be organized
   workflow, as well as the importance of his work.
   In order to develop the necessary skills of young specialist in further
   work use a set of special training and work assignments.
   Research findings show that the majority of the staff adapted to the
   professional activities, but a low level of social security indicates a
   lack of collective training and other activities.},
