   Turkish Acad Sci; Bulgarian Ind Assoc; Bulgarian Minist Environm \&
   Water},
Abstract = {Legal requirements for wastewater restitution impose quality parameters,
   which can be obtained by treatment processes; there is no assessment of
   the impact of treatment measures on local human environment and society.
   Rural communities, who have as main activity object the agriculture and
   small industry derived, face with water quality standards applied to the
   industries and urban communities. The paper aims to help the small local
   producers of agricultural products by developing a wastewater treatment
   technology based on the action of activated sludge biological
   coagulation, avoiding the use of classic coagulants (based on iron and
   aluminum salts). The described variant involves obtaining organic sludge
   containing no metals, particularly no residual heavy metals.
   Stabilization of those slurries can provide a good quality fertilizer
   and biogas obtaining. It is therefore proposed a simplified wastewater
   treatment technology that satisfies the query efficiency and ensures
   high reliability, as applicable technologies for rural communities must
   be based on simplicity, minimal resources and minimal operation staff
   training.},
