Note = {25th AGILE Conference on Geographic Information Science - Artificial
   Intelligence in the Service of Geospatial Technologies, Vilnius,
   LITHUANIA, JUN 14-17, 2022},
Organization = {AGILE},
Abstract = {Just In Time Adaptive Interventions (JITAI) are a class of applications
   that provide tailored support at the right time and place to help people
   to maintain a healthy lifestyle. This paper presents the initial version
   of a JITAI application that helps users to make healthy food choices
   when walking in an urban environment. The app provides interventions
   based on location, time, and user characteristics. It adapts its
   interventions based on the type and goal of a user. The JITAI consist of
   an app for a mobile phone and a backend server. Using the backend,
   decision points and interventions can be managed as well as users.
   Moreover, it stores tracks and intervention data. A two-phased
   experiment will be set-up. The first phase will test the robustness and
   functionality of the application with a limited number of users. Based
   on this, the app will be adapted. The second phase will test the
   effectiveness of the different type of interventions by involving a
   large user group.},
