Organization = {UNESCO; PWMTA; FAO, Netherlands},
Abstract = {China is a country suffering severe soil erosion. The total eroded area
   in the country is about 4.92 x 10(6) km(2) (1.79 x 10(6) km(2) --water
   erosion, 1.88 x 10(6) km(2) --wind erosion, and 1.25 x 10(6) km2
   --freeze-thaw erosion). The average soil erosion amount caused by water
   erosion is ca. (5-7) x 10(9) t year(-1). The eroded area may be
   classified into 5 regions according to the soil characters. Each region
   has its own features of erosion and temporal variability. Soil erosion
   has brought about serious consequences: loss of farmland, degeneration
   of soil quality, aggradation of rivers, reservoirs and lakes, hazard for
   navigation: deterioration of urban environment etc. Extensive works for
   soil and water conservation have been conducted in China with great
   success. The main approaches for control of soil erosion include
   technical measures, social and nonstructural measures, and comprehensive
   watershed management.},
