Note = {27th Congress of the International-Association-for-Hydraulic-Research,
   SAN FRANCISCO, CA, AUG 10-15, 1997},
Organization = {Int Assoc Hydraul Res},
Abstract = {About 100 years ago, the Wien River was regulated. The stone-covered
   river bed has approximately rectangular cross-sections with a small
   minor bed. Now the river should be rehabilitated. The tasks of the
   rehabilitation project are: flood protection, improvement of the
   ecosystem and the water quality, creation of a recreational area and
   redesign of the urban environment. The new river bed was developed
   utilizing hydraulic models both in the laboratory and in the Wien River.
   The bed of the ``new{''} Wien River consists of one layer of big quarry
   stones, with the gaps between the stones being filled with finer
   substratum. The filling material serves as root zone for vegetation,
   development area for benthos, and as bed load in case of floods. The
   structural elements used are dispersed bottom sills, groynes, bed
   groynes, little islands and disturbance stones (stable big stones on the
   river bed).
   The present paper gives a general view of the project and outlines the
   methods and results.},
