Abstract = {Similar to many other urban cities, food waste constitutes a large
   portion of municipal solid waste disposal in Hong Kong. Currently
   landfilling is the major disposal method, which is considered not
   sustainable because of concerns on land resource intake and potential
   long term environmental burdens. In search for more sustainable
   management of food waste, the HKSAR Government has commissioned a pilot
   biodegradable waste treatment facility in 2008 for trial recycling of
   food waste. This paper provides the background that led to the
   development of the pilot facility. Results of the characteristics of
   food waste received and the trial operation of the pilot facility are
   presented with discussion on their implications on the planning of large
   scale scheme for sustainable food waste management in Hong Kong.},
