   Environm Technol SA},
Abstract = {A study has been conducted in order to develop a baseline of industrial
   waste amount and type generated. Data were collected from six counties
   in Southeast Florida, U.S.A., with a population of more than five
   million. The study area includes urban communities, agricultural areas
   and sensitive ecosystems. Analysis of the data documented those
   industries with high rates and/or wide variety of wastes produced, the
   variability of waste generating rates, and other pertinent features. The
   study included multi-media waste (gaseous, liquid and solid) with
   emphasis on hazardous materials. The results documented the strengths
   and weaknesses of the existing industrial waste databases and identified
   areas needing further research for promoting industrial pollution
   prevention practices.},
