   1992},
Abstract = {The evolution of urban aerosol size distribution growing by
   heterogeneous reactions has been observed in winter fog. Particle
   diameter growth rates from such data are presented. The functional
   dependence of the growth rates on particle diameter infer clues about
   chemical mechanisms of heterogeneous interaction. The data are
   consistent with aerosol formation in winter fog resulting from
   condensation of low vapor pressure species formed by gas phase reactions
   and droplet phase reactions.},
