   Smart Urban Coastal Sustainabil; Tech Univ Civil Engn Bucharest, Fac
   Civil, Ind \& Agr Construct; Sustainable Solut Energy \& Environm},
Abstract = {The energy consumption in buildings, transportation, services or
   processes has been raising constantly in the last years becoming top
   priority in research fields. As its impact on the environment has become
   more and more obvious, the transportation sector has been searching for
   solutions to lower its influence on future generations. Electric
   vehicles, proposed as an alternative to the internal combustion engine
   vehicles, still face some difficulties in driving range, cost, and for
   colder climates, passenger comfort conditions. As the HVAC system
   represents the highest energy consumption from the auxiliary systems in
   electric vehicles, this paper proposes to analyse to condensation
   phenomenon inside the vehicle's cabin, especially on the windshield. The
   numerical approach assesses several scenarios of air velocities,
   temperatures, and thermal power inputs in order to establish the best
   configuration at the lowest energy cost.},
