   Sci Nonlinear Sci; Shanghai Univ; Shanghai Soc Nonlinar Sci; Tongji
   Univ; Xian Jiaotong Univ; Zhejiang Univ},
Abstract = {We studied the conditions for joint information processing of a learning
   retina implant and central visual system in humans with normal vision in
   preparation of future retina implant applications in the blind. The
   visual system was modeled by a retina module (RM) as a learning Retina
   Encoder (RE) with spatio-temporal (ST) filters and a central visual
   system module (VM). RE performs a mapping of an optical pattern PI from
   the physical- onto a neural domain, whereas VM performs a mapping from
   the neural- onto the perceptual domain and yields a visual percept P2.
   Our simulation results suggest that the elicitation of `Gestalt'
   percepts may be improved by dialog-based RE tuning with evolutionary
   algorithms and by simulated miniature eye movements. However,
   considerable efforts in neuroinformatics are still needed to elucidate
   not only the algorithmic representation of data ill the neural domain
   but also its enigmatic mapping onto the perceptual domain.},
