   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Valtellina is a valley of glacial origin located in the Central Alps
   (Northern Italy). In the past the lateral tributaries formed numerous
   alluvial fans at the exit from the valley gorges in the valley bottom.
   Due to their favourable location, alluvial fans are increasingly subject
   to human activities. However, they represent a very hazardous site as
   regards flow torrent and inundation phenomena, and thus, constitute a
   serious risk both for the urban centers and the population. A general
   morphometric characterization of the 60 main alluvial fans in Valtellina
   is provided in the paper and a more detailed research regarding 7 fans
   is presented. The activity of these fans, whose dramatic consequences
   were observed during the latest 1911 and 1987 events, demonstrated the
   existing risk. The hazard was assessed by means of an historical
   research; the elements at risk and their change over time were defined
   through the analysis of various maps. Finally, the risk was estimated by
   taking into account the change in vulnerability following the
   application of remedial measures.},
