   Univ; Swedish Univ Agr Sci},
Abstract = {In this article I illustrate and briefly describe the main
   characteristics of concept cells; that means, neurons in the human
   medial temporal lobe that respond selectively to specific concepts, like
   a particular person, place or object. Given the converging evidence on
   the behavior of concept cells and the well-known role of the medial
   temporal lobe in declarative memory, I argue that concept cells are the
   building blocks of declarative memory functions.},
