   JAPANESE NEURAL NETWORK SOCIETY - PROCEEDINGS, VOLS 1-3},
Year = {1998},
Pages = {1490-1493},
Note = {5th International Conference on Neural Information Processing (ICONIP
   98) / 1998 Annual Conference of the Japanese-Neural-Network-Society
   (JNNS 98), KITAKYUSHU, JAPAN, OCT 21-23, 1998},
Organization = {Japanese Neural Network Soc; Asian Pacific Neural Network Assembly},
Abstract = {Music and speech perception demonstrates the ability to track and attend
   to complex temporal patterns. This paper describes a simplified model of
   auditory attention that is based on the concept of an adaptive
   oscillator that adjusts phase and frequency to match the temporal
   patterning of stimulus onsets. The model explains the pattern of
   responses in categorical judgments of short temporal intervals,
   characteristic of music and speech patterns. A. link is demonstrated
   between fast and slow tempos, short and long durations, and early and
   late stimulus onsets relative to an established rhythm. The model
   illustrates the importance of rhythm and expectancy in attending to
   auditory patterns.},
