   Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 15-17, 2016},
Abstract = {To meet the demands of the urban social economy as well as to provide
   leisure and entertainment for the population, it is essential to
   maintain the health and natural operation of urban river ecosystems. In
   2011-2015, results from consecutive quarterly studies of 10 districts in
   Shanghai with more than 50 river ecological surveys and nearly 200
   sampling sites note that the Youyi river and its six river ecological
   conditions can serve as a reference point in the river ecosystem
   evaluation model of Shanghai, which includes water quality, ecological
   system and ecological landscape, and 17 indexes of the Shanghai river
   ecological evaluation index system. Based on the results and using the
   Shanghai reference point, the river ecosystem evaluation results, which
   ranged from 3.25 to 4.28, showed that its ecological conditions were
   classified under general condition; however, after the ecological
   management of the beam house bay river, its ecological conditions
   changed to relatively healthy. The evaluation index system can provide a
   reference for the health assessments of other urban rivers.},
